1
00:00:01,001 --> 00:00:03,169
♪ <i>Oh, Mr. Tailor</i> ♪

2
00:00:03,253 --> 00:00:07,215
["Mr. Tailor" playing]

3
00:00:08,508 --> 00:00:10,510
- <i>♪ Fix this</i> ♪
- <i>♪ Oh, Mr. Tailor</i> ♪

4
00:00:10,593 --> 00:00:12,679
♪ <i>Holding the scissors</i> ♪

5
00:00:12,762 --> 00:00:16,266
♪ <i>One cut, and it's settled</i> ♪

6
00:00:16,766 --> 00:00:18,143
He's searching for something.

7
00:00:18,226 --> 00:00:20,020
But he doesn't know how.

8
00:00:20,103 --> 00:00:23,523
[Kurt] <i>I saw the thief on the CCTV!</i>

9
00:00:23,606 --> 00:00:24,774
How can you be sure?

10
00:00:24,858 --> 00:00:27,610
[Kurt] <i>The diamond tattoos on his fingers!</i>

11
00:00:27,694 --> 00:00:28,778
In fairness, you're sharp.

12
00:00:28,862 --> 00:00:29,821
If he already has five million,

13
00:00:29,904 --> 00:00:31,990
why is he still vulcanizing tires
at that shop?

14
00:00:32,073 --> 00:00:33,908
[Atoy] <i>Pretend to be customers,</i>
<i>or whatever you want.</i>

15
00:00:33,992 --> 00:00:35,452
<i>What matters is you get inside.</i>

16
00:00:35,535 --> 00:00:36,453
Patch!

17
00:00:36,536 --> 00:00:37,996
Mmm. [smirks]

18
00:00:38,079 --> 00:00:39,372
- Yes. [in English] Hello, boss!
- [Emerson, in Italian] Yes.

19
00:00:39,456 --> 00:00:41,916
[Boyet] <i>Yes. Your suitcase is here.</i>

20
00:00:42,000 --> 00:00:44,085
<i>The money is safe. Don't worry.</i>

21
00:00:44,169 --> 00:00:45,795
<i>So, boss? Do you want me to count it?</i>

22
00:00:45,879 --> 00:00:49,215
[Emerson, in English] <i>Athena Hotel,</i>
<i>Olive Function Room.</i>

23
00:00:49,299 --> 00:00:50,925
<i>That's where he'll meet his Boss KM.</i>

24
00:00:51,009 --> 00:00:56,473
We need to get the money
from Boyet before he gives it to KM!

25
00:00:56,556 --> 00:00:59,934
[in English] This man
is a master of disguise.

26
00:01:00,018 --> 00:01:01,352
[in English] Do you know this man?

27
00:01:01,436 --> 00:01:02,479
‪PREVIOUSLY

28
00:01:02,562 --> 00:01:03,396
[Audrey, in English] <i>No.</i>

29
00:01:03,480 --> 00:01:06,858
[Atoy] <i>Someone must pose</i>
<i>as a buyer at the auction.</i>

30
00:01:06,941 --> 00:01:08,318
Don't involve Karla.

31
00:01:08,401 --> 00:01:09,569
[Emerson] <i>I'll handle it.</i>

32
00:01:09,652 --> 00:01:11,112
<i>We'll fix this. I'll update you.</i>

33
00:01:11,196 --> 00:01:13,239
Bring me along, please.

34
00:01:13,323 --> 00:01:16,534
I don't want to be left behind,
just worrying about you.

35
00:01:16,618 --> 00:01:19,162
Atoy will scold me. He'll be mad.

36
00:01:19,245 --> 00:01:21,414
He doesn't need to know, right?

37
00:01:21,498 --> 00:01:23,792
Come on, I'll help.

38
00:01:25,543 --> 00:01:26,461
[clicks tongue]

39
00:01:26,544 --> 00:01:30,131
[music concludes]

40
00:01:30,215 --> 00:01:31,174
Come on!

41
00:01:31,257 --> 00:01:33,718
Fine! Yes! Yes! Okay, okay!

42
00:01:33,802 --> 00:01:35,428
Go inside now.

43
00:01:36,054 --> 00:01:37,472
I'll just get something from the shop.

44
00:01:37,555 --> 00:01:39,474
When I get back,
we'll come up with a plan.

45
00:01:39,557 --> 00:01:41,142
Thank you, brother! Thanks!

46
00:01:41,226 --> 00:01:44,312
- [Emerson] You're so persistent.
- You're so handsome! Idol!

47
00:01:45,647 --> 00:01:46,564
Karla.

48
00:01:46,648 --> 00:01:48,650
- Oh?
- I'll join your mission.

49
00:01:48,733 --> 00:01:49,901
[in English] Maybe you need
one more hand.

50
00:01:49,984 --> 00:01:51,319
Psst. Keep quiet.

51
00:01:51,402 --> 00:01:54,697
They don't know you know
Brother Atoy's side job.

52
00:01:55,406 --> 00:01:58,284
And Brother Emerson won't allow it.

53
00:01:58,368 --> 00:01:59,911
You're Red Regalia's son.

54
00:01:59,994 --> 00:02:02,789
So, let's keep it a secret then.

55
00:02:02,872 --> 00:02:04,624
Oh, so it's like
a secret mission with you,

56
00:02:04,707 --> 00:02:05,875
without Brother Atoy knowing.

57
00:02:06,543 --> 00:02:08,503
You're such a gossip.

58
00:02:08,586 --> 00:02:10,755
I just overheard. Come on, Karla.

59
00:02:10,839 --> 00:02:12,257
I'll help you.

60
00:02:12,340 --> 00:02:13,883
I'll make sure you're safe.

61
00:02:13,967 --> 00:02:15,260
Come on.

62
00:02:15,802 --> 00:02:19,305
Why don't you just help Cathy?

63
00:02:19,389 --> 00:02:21,224
Maybe she's busy in the barangay.

64
00:02:21,307 --> 00:02:22,142
- Go check.
- No.

65
00:02:22,225 --> 00:02:24,269
I'd rather be with you.

66
00:02:24,352 --> 00:02:25,645
[pleasant music playing]

67
00:02:25,728 --> 00:02:26,646
- What?
- No.

68
00:02:26,729 --> 00:02:28,982
I mean, it's more exciting
to join the mission.

69
00:02:29,065 --> 00:02:31,192
- Ah. The mission.
- Right? Come on, Karla. Please.

70
00:02:33,194 --> 00:02:34,070
Fine.

71
00:02:34,154 --> 00:02:35,029
Yes!

72
00:02:35,113 --> 00:02:36,281
- [in English] Game.
- Psst.

73
00:02:36,364 --> 00:02:38,741
Just don't tell anyone.

74
00:02:38,825 --> 00:02:40,285
I'll let you know the plan.

75
00:02:40,368 --> 00:02:42,287
- [in English] Okay.
- And…

76
00:02:42,370 --> 00:02:46,207
Brother Emerson
must never know you're joining.

77
00:02:46,291 --> 00:02:48,710
[in English] Okay. Copy, boss.

78
00:02:48,793 --> 00:02:49,669
- [in English] Okay?
- [in English] Okay.

79
00:02:49,752 --> 00:02:54,465
[suave theme music playing]

80
00:02:54,549 --> 00:02:56,384
[motorcycle revving]

81
00:02:56,467 --> 00:02:57,343
[sewing machine whirring]

82
00:02:57,427 --> 00:02:58,303
[scratches]

83
00:02:58,386 --> 00:03:00,305
[snipping]

84
00:03:00,388 --> 00:03:04,183
[sewing machine clacking]

85
00:03:04,267 --> 00:03:05,894
- [gun cocks]
- [gunshots]

86
00:03:05,977 --> 00:03:07,562
[gunshots]

87
00:03:07,645 --> 00:03:09,856
[music intensifies]

88
00:03:09,939 --> 00:03:11,941
- [clicking]
- [snipping]

89
00:03:12,025 --> 00:03:13,902
[music swells]

90
00:03:17,697 --> 00:03:20,617
[music fades]

91
00:03:20,700 --> 00:03:23,870
[in English] This is composite.
It's 99% accurate.

92
00:03:23,953 --> 00:03:25,830
[in English] Why are you doubting it now?

93
00:03:26,664 --> 00:03:29,459
[in English] This is the woman
we met in the embassy.

94
00:03:29,542 --> 00:03:32,629
[in English] She's very beautiful,
that is why I doubt.

95
00:03:32,712 --> 00:03:36,049
[in English] You mentioned
that it's AI-generated, right?

96
00:03:36,132 --> 00:03:38,593
- [in English] Yes.
- [in English] So, doesn't that mean that

97
00:03:38,676 --> 00:03:41,387
there's a chance that maybe
the composition is wrong?

98
00:03:41,471 --> 00:03:43,973
[man, in English]
Is she even interested in you?

99
00:03:44,057 --> 00:03:46,100
[in English] Well, she gave me her number.

100
00:03:46,184 --> 00:03:47,435
[in English] So, yes.

101
00:03:47,518 --> 00:03:49,145
[in English] Why don't you just call her

102
00:03:49,229 --> 00:03:51,147
and stop questioning my skills?

103
00:03:51,231 --> 00:03:52,982
[pensive music playing]

104
00:03:53,066 --> 00:03:54,150
[in English] I will.

105
00:04:00,907 --> 00:04:04,953
[line ringing]

106
00:04:07,664 --> 00:04:08,665
Hello?

107
00:04:10,166 --> 00:04:13,628
[in English] Hello, Ms. Audrey.
This is Samir.

108
00:04:13,711 --> 00:04:17,131
[in English] I know
that we, uh, just spoke,

109
00:04:17,215 --> 00:04:21,302
but I'd like to know
if you'd want to go on a date?

110
00:04:21,386 --> 00:04:22,387
Oh!

111
00:04:23,221 --> 00:04:24,389
[in English] Really?!

112
00:04:25,223 --> 00:04:27,308
[in English] See. She likes me.

113
00:04:27,392 --> 00:04:29,644
[playful music playing]

114
00:04:29,727 --> 00:04:32,105
[in English] Ah, when are you available?

115
00:04:32,188 --> 00:04:34,232
[in English] Anytime!

116
00:04:34,315 --> 00:04:35,525
[in English] Anytime?

117
00:04:35,608 --> 00:04:36,985
[in English] Really?

118
00:04:37,068 --> 00:04:39,821
[in English] Why do you sound
different, Ms. Audrey?

119
00:04:39,904 --> 00:04:40,738
[giggles]

120
00:04:40,822 --> 00:04:43,700
[in English] Actually, I'm not Audrey.

121
00:04:43,783 --> 00:04:47,328
[in English] But I am single
and available just for you!

122
00:04:47,412 --> 00:04:49,330
Wait. Are you AFAM?

123
00:04:49,414 --> 00:04:51,791
Because my nose is bleeding
from all this English.

124
00:04:51,874 --> 00:04:53,626
I need subtitles.

125
00:04:53,710 --> 00:04:55,044
[in English] Wait. Who is this?

126
00:04:55,128 --> 00:04:56,004
[Jona on the phone] <i>Okay.</i>

127
00:04:56,087 --> 00:04:58,464
He really speaks in English…

128
00:04:58,548 --> 00:05:00,591
Well, fine. I'm ready to fight.

129
00:05:00,675 --> 00:05:05,888
[in English] Um, my name
is Jose Bernardo Carandang!

130
00:05:05,972 --> 00:05:08,725
[Jona on the phone, in English]
<i>You can call me Jona!</i>

131
00:05:08,808 --> 00:05:12,353
[in English] I'm 22 years old,
from the place where religious

132
00:05:12,437 --> 00:05:16,190
devotion meets affordable shopping!

133
00:05:16,274 --> 00:05:18,735
Baclaran!

134
00:05:18,818 --> 00:05:21,070
[in English] Hey, is this, uh…

135
00:05:21,154 --> 00:05:27,827
0900-020001-00?

136
00:05:27,910 --> 00:05:29,620
[in English] Correct!

137
00:05:29,704 --> 00:05:33,374
[in English] I think
this is destiny, mister--

138
00:05:35,251 --> 00:05:36,669
- [in English] Hello?
- [quirky blipping]

139
00:05:38,004 --> 00:05:39,255
[in English] Hello?!

140
00:05:39,964 --> 00:05:41,799
[in English] She gave you
a different number.

141
00:05:42,425 --> 00:05:43,551
[in English] Yes, she did.

142
00:05:44,761 --> 00:05:47,388
[in English] Maybe she's not
over her ex or something.

143
00:05:47,472 --> 00:05:48,848
[in English] Just forget about her.

144
00:05:49,724 --> 00:05:54,729
[suspicious music playing]

145
00:05:55,813 --> 00:05:57,065
What's this?!

146
00:05:57,148 --> 00:05:59,317
That was an AFAM. Now he's gone!

147
00:05:59,400 --> 00:06:01,861
Who were you talking to, Jona?

148
00:06:01,944 --> 00:06:04,113
Exactly. You've been speaking
English nonstop.

149
00:06:04,197 --> 00:06:05,698
I almost ran out!

150
00:06:05,782 --> 00:06:07,325
Almost!

151
00:06:07,408 --> 00:06:10,661
Um, wrong number. Looking for…

152
00:06:10,745 --> 00:06:12,038
Audrey?

153
00:06:12,789 --> 00:06:13,790
Audrey?

154
00:06:14,457 --> 00:06:16,209
- Audrey?
- True.

155
00:06:16,834 --> 00:06:19,587
Isn't that the name
of Brother Atoy's girlfriend?

156
00:06:19,670 --> 00:06:20,505
Yes.

157
00:06:20,588 --> 00:06:23,216
You're late on the news!

158
00:06:23,299 --> 00:06:25,802
They're not together anymore!
They broke up!

159
00:06:25,885 --> 00:06:27,220
[Jona] Oh, really?

160
00:06:27,303 --> 00:06:29,514
Is that confirmed, Siony?

161
00:06:29,597 --> 00:06:31,140
I'm not sure.

162
00:06:31,224 --> 00:06:33,017
But that's the rumor.

163
00:06:33,101 --> 00:06:34,852
What a shame.

164
00:06:34,936 --> 00:06:37,146
They looked good together.

165
00:06:37,730 --> 00:06:39,148
Like me and Emerson.

166
00:06:39,232 --> 00:06:41,692
- Oh. Gosh, girl.
- [Mona] You brought up Emerson again.

167
00:06:41,776 --> 00:06:42,944
She had to connect it.

168
00:06:43,027 --> 00:06:45,947
- She's really head over heels.
- [Jona] Mmm-mmm. Crazy.

169
00:06:46,030 --> 00:06:48,199
[Mona] Oh, oh, oh.

170
00:06:56,082 --> 00:06:59,752
[in English] We have information.
Ms. Lily Santiago, no longer in Manila.

171
00:06:59,836 --> 00:07:01,212
[in English] We are still looking for her.

172
00:07:01,295 --> 00:07:03,756
[in English] What about the man
who broke into the embassy?

173
00:07:03,840 --> 00:07:04,674
[in English] Did you find him?

174
00:07:04,757 --> 00:07:08,052
[in English] We shared his photo
with our security team.

175
00:07:08,928 --> 00:07:10,847
[in English] The man is a total mystery.

176
00:07:11,931 --> 00:07:14,142
[in English] It's harder to find him
without his name.

177
00:07:14,225 --> 00:07:18,438
[in English] We might need
an expert tracker to find this guy.

178
00:07:20,356 --> 00:07:21,399
Viktor.

179
00:07:23,067 --> 00:07:25,111
[in English] I value our friendship.

180
00:07:25,653 --> 00:07:28,406
[in English] I will never
steal anything from you!

181
00:07:28,906 --> 00:07:32,660
[in English] If you want,
I can help you find this man.

182
00:07:33,244 --> 00:07:37,123
[in English] I know
a very good tracker, a man hunter.

183
00:07:37,206 --> 00:07:41,544
[suspicious music playing]

184
00:07:45,798 --> 00:07:47,884
[line rings]

185
00:07:49,886 --> 00:07:51,304
[in English] Hello, Ambassador.

186
00:07:52,472 --> 00:07:57,310
[in English] We have a slight problem
with the man who broke into the embassy.

187
00:07:57,393 --> 00:08:00,563
[in English] I think
we need Mr. Dmitri's help.

188
00:08:00,646 --> 00:08:01,689
[in English] We need a tracker.

189
00:08:01,772 --> 00:08:04,609
[tense music playing]

190
00:08:04,692 --> 00:08:08,696
Karla, how's your application
to be an usher?

191
00:08:08,779 --> 00:08:10,948
Here it is, brother. I already applied.

192
00:08:11,032 --> 00:08:12,617
[in English] Usher intern.

193
00:08:12,700 --> 00:08:14,076
- Hmm.
- [Emerson, in English] Very good.

194
00:08:14,160 --> 00:08:15,870
As for me, I'll be a waiter.

195
00:08:16,370 --> 00:08:17,538
I'll go in as a waiter,

196
00:08:17,622 --> 00:08:20,833
so I can observe their movements.

197
00:08:20,917 --> 00:08:22,835
What about the clothing for me
and Brother Kurt?

198
00:08:22,919 --> 00:08:24,212
I'll handle that.

199
00:08:24,295 --> 00:08:26,130
By tomorrow, everything will be ready.

200
00:08:26,964 --> 00:08:31,594
Remember, our target is Boss KM.

201
00:08:32,929 --> 00:08:34,388
Kevin Martinez.

202
00:08:35,640 --> 00:08:38,434
And the suitcase with five million pesos.

203
00:08:40,895 --> 00:08:42,480
[in English] Five million pesos.

204
00:08:42,563 --> 00:08:45,566
We better rest now
so we can go full force tomorrow.

205
00:08:45,650 --> 00:08:46,651
[Karla] I agree.

206
00:08:46,734 --> 00:08:47,944
[Emerson] Wait.

207
00:08:48,027 --> 00:08:49,070
[quirky warp]

208
00:08:52,073 --> 00:08:53,407
What's this?

209
00:08:54,242 --> 00:08:55,660
You'll wear that.

210
00:08:55,743 --> 00:08:59,705
It's the uniform
of Atoy's new breakout group.

211
00:09:00,248 --> 00:09:04,043
The Children of the Thread,
led by yours truly.

212
00:09:04,126 --> 00:09:05,920
[sneaky music playing]

213
00:09:06,003 --> 00:09:06,921
[in English] Me.

214
00:09:07,964 --> 00:09:09,215
This is all we'll wear?

215
00:09:09,298 --> 00:09:10,758
Of course not!

216
00:09:11,259 --> 00:09:13,052
We'll layer it.

217
00:09:13,135 --> 00:09:15,930
But suspenders are required.

218
00:09:16,013 --> 00:09:18,140
Go on, put them on!

219
00:09:18,224 --> 00:09:20,184
- This is Emerson's baby!
- [Emerson] No…

220
00:09:20,268 --> 00:09:21,769
Don't-- It won't be seen.

221
00:09:21,852 --> 00:09:23,771
It's our brand identity!

222
00:09:24,689 --> 00:09:27,400
We need to look solid
for our first mission.

223
00:09:28,234 --> 00:09:29,569
[Karla] How do we attach this?

224
00:09:29,652 --> 00:09:31,195
[mid-tempo rock music playing]

225
00:09:31,279 --> 00:09:35,199
The Operation Suitcase.

226
00:09:35,283 --> 00:09:37,118
[huffs]

227
00:09:37,201 --> 00:09:38,619
[Karla] Let's try it.

228
00:09:38,703 --> 00:09:39,787
Does this go at the back?

229
00:09:41,539 --> 00:09:43,040
- [Karla] Feels like a backpack.
- [Ame] It's tight.

230
00:09:43,124 --> 00:09:44,417
Oh.

231
00:09:45,626 --> 00:09:46,627
Okay.

232
00:09:47,587 --> 00:09:49,213
- Let's take a group selfie.
- Hmm?

233
00:09:49,297 --> 00:09:50,423
Yes, send it to Atoy.

234
00:09:50,506 --> 00:09:52,967
No, I'll take the picture.
I can't be seen.

235
00:09:53,050 --> 00:09:54,176
- Join the next one.
- Okay, okay, okay, okay.

236
00:09:54,260 --> 00:09:55,553
- [Emerson] Next time.
- [Ame] Yes.

237
00:09:55,636 --> 00:09:57,430
- [Emerson] Okay.
- There, 1.5, 2.5.

238
00:09:57,513 --> 00:09:58,514
Hold it like this.

239
00:09:58,598 --> 00:09:59,473
You hold it, Ame.

240
00:09:59,557 --> 00:10:02,393
- Oh! Then I'll be the only one visible.
- Brother, come on.

241
00:10:02,476 --> 00:10:03,728
Okay, okay. Fine, fine.

242
00:10:03,811 --> 00:10:05,062
- [in English] Okay.
- Fix it!

243
00:10:05,146 --> 00:10:07,398
- I'm not visible!
- Wait, I can't see Sis Ame.

244
00:10:07,481 --> 00:10:08,649
- Hurry!
- Adjust, adjust. Adjust, correct!

245
00:10:08,733 --> 00:10:10,151
0.5, right?

246
00:10:10,234 --> 00:10:12,069
- [overlapping chatter]
- There, there! That's it.

247
00:10:12,153 --> 00:10:12,987
[Emerson] We're all visible now.

248
00:10:13,070 --> 00:10:14,905
[in English] Smile! One, two, three.

249
00:10:14,989 --> 00:10:17,116
- [camera shutter snaps]
- [Karla, in English] Yes!

250
00:10:17,199 --> 00:10:19,952
That's cute! Ohh!

251
00:10:20,036 --> 00:10:21,078
Okay, okay, okay.

252
00:10:21,162 --> 00:10:22,622
- [Ame] Oh, with you this time.
- [Emerson] Join in, join in.

253
00:10:22,705 --> 00:10:25,041
- We won't send it to Atoy.
- [overlapping chatter]

254
00:10:25,124 --> 00:10:26,459
- [in English] Okay.
- Wait, wait.

255
00:10:26,542 --> 00:10:27,627
Let's check.

256
00:10:27,710 --> 00:10:29,587
Everybody say, Children of the Thread.

257
00:10:29,670 --> 00:10:31,297
[all] Children of the Thread!

258
00:10:31,380 --> 00:10:33,049
- [camera shutter snaps] Child of Emerson!
- Oh, no.

259
00:10:33,132 --> 00:10:34,300
- [giggles]
- [camera shutter snaps]

260
00:10:34,383 --> 00:10:36,052
[music ends]

261
00:10:36,969 --> 00:10:39,180
[phone blips]

262
00:10:39,263 --> 00:10:41,515
SIS AME

263
00:10:47,146 --> 00:10:50,733
[melancholic music playing]

264
00:10:50,816 --> 00:10:55,655
[phone ringing]

265
00:10:57,031 --> 00:10:58,783
Hello, Sis Ame?

266
00:10:58,866 --> 00:11:01,827
Did you see the picture I sent?

267
00:11:01,911 --> 00:11:04,038
Yes, but…

268
00:11:04,580 --> 00:11:07,375
why are you all wearing the same outfit?

269
00:11:07,458 --> 00:11:09,877
We have a mission tomorrow.

270
00:11:09,960 --> 00:11:11,212
Atoy isn't here.

271
00:11:11,295 --> 00:11:12,922
He has another assignment,

272
00:11:13,005 --> 00:11:14,840
so we'll handle it instead.

273
00:11:14,924 --> 00:11:17,134
The Children of the Thread!

274
00:11:17,218 --> 00:11:20,012
Children of the Thread?

275
00:11:22,348 --> 00:11:23,307
Wait.

276
00:11:23,808 --> 00:11:26,977
Why am I not included?

277
00:11:27,061 --> 00:11:30,398
I'm the OG Child of the Thread of Tatoy.

278
00:11:30,481 --> 00:11:31,357
Yes, of course.

279
00:11:31,440 --> 00:11:34,485
You're the original Child of the Thread.

280
00:11:34,568 --> 00:11:39,323
But Tatoy won't allow you
to join the mission.

281
00:11:39,407 --> 00:11:41,867
It's better you stay safe with your mom.

282
00:11:42,535 --> 00:11:43,994
Okay.

283
00:11:44,078 --> 00:11:46,205
Why do you sound sad? How are you there?

284
00:11:46,288 --> 00:11:47,957
How's Mama Olga?

285
00:11:48,624 --> 00:11:50,418
I'm okay.

286
00:11:51,502 --> 00:11:55,423
But I miss you.

287
00:11:56,006 --> 00:11:58,342
I miss you too, Ibyang.

288
00:11:58,426 --> 00:12:02,596
Mmm, promise. I'll call you tomorrow
when our mission succeeds.

289
00:12:02,680 --> 00:12:04,390
I'll tell you everything.

290
00:12:04,473 --> 00:12:06,267
Just behave there, okay?

291
00:12:06,892 --> 00:12:08,602
[in English] Always, Sis Ame.

292
00:12:29,331 --> 00:12:34,503
[sneaky music playing]

293
00:12:44,930 --> 00:12:46,140
Oh?

294
00:12:46,223 --> 00:12:47,933
I thought you threw that away.

295
00:12:48,809 --> 00:12:50,478
You finished it instead.

296
00:12:51,645 --> 00:12:52,855
Not yet.

297
00:12:53,939 --> 00:12:56,817
I'm just finishing the handle.

298
00:12:57,776 --> 00:13:00,279
Why did you still work on it?

299
00:13:01,864 --> 00:13:05,201
It would be a waste.

300
00:13:06,243 --> 00:13:08,329
You worked hard on it.

301
00:13:08,871 --> 00:13:12,458
Besides, once I finish this,

302
00:13:12,541 --> 00:13:15,503
it's like we both made it together!

303
00:13:15,586 --> 00:13:16,629
Right?

304
00:13:16,712 --> 00:13:19,673
[melancholic music playing]

305
00:13:19,757 --> 00:13:21,300
Okay. [clears throat]

306
00:13:21,383 --> 00:13:24,053
Thank you for doing that.

307
00:13:24,136 --> 00:13:26,764
So, to make it even,
so I can make it up to you,

308
00:13:26,847 --> 00:13:29,517
I'll cook our breakfast. Hmm?

309
00:13:29,600 --> 00:13:31,936
- What do you want?
- Anything.

310
00:13:32,520 --> 00:13:33,354
Hmm…

311
00:13:33,437 --> 00:13:35,481
All right, instant noodles, then.

312
00:13:35,564 --> 00:13:40,277
But Tatoy said breakfast
should be nutritious.

313
00:13:40,945 --> 00:13:42,154
So…

314
00:13:43,030 --> 00:13:44,240
I'll add an egg.

315
00:13:44,782 --> 00:13:46,158
Okay?

316
00:13:47,243 --> 00:13:52,873
[sentimental music playing]

317
00:13:57,920 --> 00:14:00,965
[music fades]

318
00:14:04,718 --> 00:14:05,719
[knocks on door]

319
00:14:05,803 --> 00:14:07,012
Anyone home?

320
00:14:07,096 --> 00:14:09,139
Hey, Audrey.

321
00:14:09,682 --> 00:14:10,683
You're early!

322
00:14:11,225 --> 00:14:12,977
Hi, Ame. Um…

323
00:14:14,520 --> 00:14:17,022
Is Atoy here?

324
00:14:17,106 --> 00:14:18,857
I want to talk to him.

325
00:14:18,941 --> 00:14:21,110
He left. He has work.

326
00:14:21,193 --> 00:14:22,444
You know how it is.

327
00:14:22,528 --> 00:14:23,863
[melancholic music playing]

328
00:14:23,946 --> 00:14:24,989
Ah.

329
00:14:25,906 --> 00:14:26,949
Um…

330
00:14:29,577 --> 00:14:31,871
I wanted to say goodbye

331
00:14:32,580 --> 00:14:33,789
because…

332
00:14:34,331 --> 00:14:36,041
Janine and I are leaving.

333
00:14:36,917 --> 00:14:38,878
We're going to the US.

334
00:14:39,670 --> 00:14:40,880
Hmm, vacation?

335
00:14:41,463 --> 00:14:42,506
[in English] Maybe.

336
00:14:44,383 --> 00:14:45,843
[in English] Maybe for good.

337
00:14:45,926 --> 00:14:47,469
[sighs] Ah.

338
00:14:47,553 --> 00:14:50,681
Just call or text him.

339
00:14:53,976 --> 00:14:55,895
What about Ibyang?

340
00:14:55,978 --> 00:14:57,313
Is she here?

341
00:14:57,396 --> 00:15:01,567
I brought cookies for her.

342
00:15:01,650 --> 00:15:04,236
I also want to say goodbye.

343
00:15:04,820 --> 00:15:05,946
Ah.

344
00:15:06,030 --> 00:15:08,407
Ibyang's not here anymore.

345
00:15:08,490 --> 00:15:09,658
[in English] For good.

346
00:15:11,035 --> 00:15:11,869
What?

347
00:15:11,952 --> 00:15:13,412
Why?

348
00:15:13,495 --> 00:15:14,955
Where is she?

349
00:15:15,664 --> 00:15:19,084
Her real mother took her.

350
00:15:21,003 --> 00:15:22,004
What?

351
00:15:23,547 --> 00:15:24,840
Who is she?

352
00:15:26,050 --> 00:15:28,093
[in English] Is she a good person?

353
00:15:28,177 --> 00:15:29,845
[in English] Is Atoy okay with it?

354
00:15:30,721 --> 00:15:33,474
Does he trust her?
Why did she only show up now?

355
00:15:33,557 --> 00:15:34,642
[scoffs]

356
00:15:34,725 --> 00:15:38,938
You know, you're asking
the same questions Atoy asked Olga.

357
00:15:39,438 --> 00:15:43,442
Better open those cookies.

358
00:15:43,943 --> 00:15:46,528
I'll make us coffee

359
00:15:46,612 --> 00:15:49,698
because this will be a long talk.

360
00:15:49,782 --> 00:15:51,241
Mmm-mmm.

361
00:15:51,325 --> 00:15:53,744
This must be what Ibyang mentioned.

362
00:15:55,162 --> 00:15:58,332
So, her name is Olga?

363
00:15:58,832 --> 00:16:00,042
Hmm? Mm-mmm.

364
00:16:01,669 --> 00:16:02,795
They taste good, right?

365
00:16:02,878 --> 00:16:05,798
[music fades]

366
00:16:05,881 --> 00:16:11,845
[phone ringing]

367
00:16:15,641 --> 00:16:17,393
[in English] Good morning!

368
00:16:17,476 --> 00:16:21,563
Wow, my favorite person
in the world called so early.

369
00:16:21,647 --> 00:16:22,856
[in English] What's up, Director?

370
00:16:22,940 --> 00:16:24,149
[in English] Hello, Olga.

371
00:16:24,233 --> 00:16:27,111
Come to my set. I need extras.

372
00:16:27,194 --> 00:16:28,278
Huh?

373
00:16:28,362 --> 00:16:30,614
I have a gig now.

374
00:16:30,698 --> 00:16:31,824
I can't.

375
00:16:31,907 --> 00:16:34,159
[director on the phone] <i>Ah, too bad, but…</i>

376
00:16:34,243 --> 00:16:38,872
- I have producer friends from the US here.
- [sneaky music playing]

377
00:16:38,956 --> 00:16:41,542
They're looking for new talents.

378
00:16:41,625 --> 00:16:44,712
<i>Who knows, maybe this is</i>
<i>your chance to be famous!</i>

379
00:16:44,795 --> 00:16:45,671
Really?

380
00:16:46,588 --> 00:16:50,175
You know I've dreamed of that for so long.

381
00:16:50,259 --> 00:16:53,637
Why now? When I'm full-time at this job?

382
00:16:53,721 --> 00:16:54,555
Okay, fine.

383
00:16:54,638 --> 00:16:56,265
Should I give the chance to someone else?

384
00:16:56,348 --> 00:16:57,933
Wait.

385
00:16:58,017 --> 00:16:59,685
[sneaky music playing]

386
00:16:59,768 --> 00:17:00,602
[frustrated grunt]

387
00:17:00,686 --> 00:17:04,565
Um, where is it?

388
00:17:04,648 --> 00:17:07,192
You're quick to give it away, Director.

389
00:17:07,276 --> 00:17:09,611
[director on the phone]
<i>At the mall! Near your house.</i>

390
00:17:09,695 --> 00:17:11,572
Come on. Move!

391
00:17:11,655 --> 00:17:12,614
Okay. Fine, fine.

392
00:17:12,698 --> 00:17:14,366
I'll go there. Okay?

393
00:17:14,450 --> 00:17:16,076
[in English] Okay, Director.
See you. Bye-bye!

394
00:17:16,160 --> 00:17:18,037
- [phone blips]
- Ibyang.

395
00:17:18,120 --> 00:17:20,080
Take charge of what I'm cooking, okay?

396
00:17:20,164 --> 00:17:22,624
It just needs seasoning. You know how.

397
00:17:23,459 --> 00:17:25,294
Can I come with you?

398
00:17:25,377 --> 00:17:27,254
Huh? No way!

399
00:17:27,337 --> 00:17:28,422
Stay here!

400
00:17:29,048 --> 00:17:30,299
[upbeat sneaky music playing]

401
00:17:30,382 --> 00:17:31,216
[Olga exclaims excitedly]

402
00:17:42,811 --> 00:17:44,480
Do you think what we're going
to do later will be hard?

403
00:17:44,563 --> 00:17:45,773
Looks like it'll be easy.

404
00:17:45,856 --> 00:17:48,275
- Really? Really? Okay.
- [man 1] We'll handle it.

405
00:17:48,358 --> 00:17:49,193
Bye-bye.

406
00:17:49,902 --> 00:17:50,861
[man] Let me just call the director.

407
00:17:50,944 --> 00:17:52,988
Psst, psst. Friend!

408
00:17:53,072 --> 00:17:55,157
Hey! Wait. What are you doing here?

409
00:17:55,240 --> 00:17:56,116
Hmm? Why?

410
00:17:56,200 --> 00:17:58,994
I thought your wallet was already thick.

411
00:17:59,495 --> 00:18:00,579
Where's--

412
00:18:00,662 --> 00:18:02,873
- Who?
- Where's-- Where's the little one?

413
00:18:03,373 --> 00:18:05,125
She's not here. She's at home.

414
00:18:05,209 --> 00:18:08,962
What? You left her? Alone?

415
00:18:09,046 --> 00:18:12,466
- Sis, you prioritized taping.
- My God. What's this?

416
00:18:12,549 --> 00:18:13,759
She can handle herself.

417
00:18:13,842 --> 00:18:15,385
Don't worry too much.

418
00:18:15,469 --> 00:18:17,888
Besides, I won't miss this.

419
00:18:17,971 --> 00:18:20,390
I won't miss my chance to be famous.

420
00:18:20,474 --> 00:18:22,226
- [Charmi] Wow.
- I love my craft, you know?

421
00:18:22,893 --> 00:18:23,769
[in English] Craft.

422
00:18:23,852 --> 00:18:25,229
Wow. What happened?

423
00:18:25,312 --> 00:18:27,356
I thought this was all for money?

424
00:18:27,439 --> 00:18:29,733
Of course, that too.

425
00:18:29,817 --> 00:18:31,485
But… You know.

426
00:18:32,402 --> 00:18:33,529
Do you see that?

427
00:18:33,612 --> 00:18:36,615
- The one in the denim vest.
- [Charmi] Oh?

428
00:18:36,698 --> 00:18:38,742
- [Olga] He'll see my talent.
- [inaudible]

429
00:18:38,826 --> 00:18:40,410
He's going to be the solution,

430
00:18:40,494 --> 00:18:42,955
so I can finally get out
of being a starlet!

431
00:18:43,038 --> 00:18:44,581
[in English] I'm gonna be a star.

432
00:18:44,665 --> 00:18:46,375
[in English] I'm gonna be a superstar!

433
00:18:46,458 --> 00:18:49,086
[exclaiming]

434
00:18:49,169 --> 00:18:52,256
- [phone ringing]
- Wait, someone's calling!

435
00:18:52,339 --> 00:18:53,382
There.

436
00:18:53,882 --> 00:18:57,678
Oh, Nora Aunor called from her grave.

437
00:18:57,761 --> 00:19:00,430
She said don't steal her title!

438
00:19:00,514 --> 00:19:01,390
- Overacting.
- [giggles]

439
00:19:10,607 --> 00:19:13,235
I'll wash these later when I get home.

440
00:19:17,406 --> 00:19:19,658
Maybe Mama's hungry.

441
00:19:20,284 --> 00:19:21,493
Oh, here.

442
00:19:21,577 --> 00:19:27,040
[whimsical music playing]

443
00:19:45,017 --> 00:19:47,686
[director] Listen, listen!
Everyone, come here!

444
00:19:47,769 --> 00:19:48,770
Yes! Hi, Director!

445
00:19:48,854 --> 00:19:50,105
- [director] Where's my AD?
- Hello, Director!

446
00:19:50,189 --> 00:19:51,523
Hey, stand behind me.

447
00:19:51,607 --> 00:19:54,526
- [mutters]
- Okay, everyone.

448
00:19:54,610 --> 00:19:57,738
Here's what will happen
in the scene later.

449
00:19:57,821 --> 00:20:03,952
Armed men will massacre you!

450
00:20:04,036 --> 00:20:05,537
You'll all be terrified!

451
00:20:05,621 --> 00:20:07,539
- [gasps]
- [director] Show me fear!

452
00:20:07,623 --> 00:20:10,584
- [gasps]
- [director] And you'll be helpless.

453
00:20:10,667 --> 00:20:11,960
Then they'll shoot you all.

454
00:20:12,044 --> 00:20:13,378
[imitates gun firing sound]

455
00:20:13,462 --> 00:20:15,005
Like that! Okay?

456
00:20:15,088 --> 00:20:17,382
Are my instructions clear?

457
00:20:17,466 --> 00:20:18,884
Yes. Thank you…

458
00:20:18,967 --> 00:20:21,720
- Director! Director, is it okay
- [in English] Oh, yes, darling?

459
00:20:21,803 --> 00:20:23,430
if I suggest something?

460
00:20:23,513 --> 00:20:29,394
Because isn't it boring
if we all just agree to get shot?

461
00:20:29,478 --> 00:20:32,064
Maybe one of us could fight back?

462
00:20:32,147 --> 00:20:33,857
It can be just me.

463
00:20:33,941 --> 00:20:36,526
Is that okay, Director? Because, you know…

464
00:20:36,610 --> 00:20:38,445
To add some action.

465
00:20:38,946 --> 00:20:40,239
- I like that.
- Right?

466
00:20:40,322 --> 00:20:42,157
- Here's what I'll do, Director.
- [director] Mmm-mmm. Let's see.

467
00:20:42,241 --> 00:20:45,035
- So, when two men approach, right,
- Yes.

468
00:20:45,118 --> 00:20:46,662
- I'll jump.
- [director] Oh?

469
00:20:46,745 --> 00:20:48,664
When I jump, they'll shoot.

470
00:20:48,747 --> 00:20:51,875
I'll dodge, so it'll cramp.
The bullet will graze me.

471
00:20:51,959 --> 00:20:53,669
But others here will get hit.

472
00:20:53,752 --> 00:20:55,295
- [director] Who?
- Them, them.

473
00:20:55,379 --> 00:20:56,964
- Ah, that works.
- Yes, they can.

474
00:20:57,047 --> 00:20:59,132
- [director] Hey, take notes. Unbelievable.
- Then…

475
00:20:59,216 --> 00:21:01,009
- [director] Yes, then?
- I'll punch like this.

476
00:21:01,093 --> 00:21:03,178
- Oh, yes. Beautiful.
- Like that, okay.

477
00:21:03,262 --> 00:21:04,638
Then I'll kick like this.

478
00:21:04,721 --> 00:21:06,723
- [director] Riveting. Yes.
- Then they'll fall.

479
00:21:07,516 --> 00:21:09,351
[goon actor 1] The job would've been easy,

480
00:21:09,434 --> 00:21:11,311
but she's making it hard.

481
00:21:11,395 --> 00:21:12,396
Exactly.

482
00:21:12,479 --> 00:21:14,731
Olga's such a nuisance!

483
00:21:14,815 --> 00:21:16,108
Feeling main character!

484
00:21:16,733 --> 00:21:19,903
[goon actor 1] It doesn't matter.
She'll get killed anyway.

485
00:21:19,987 --> 00:21:22,656
Later, I'll riddle her with bullets.

486
00:21:22,739 --> 00:21:23,991
I'll use them all on her.

487
00:21:24,074 --> 00:21:25,158
[both cackle]

488
00:21:25,242 --> 00:21:26,994
- [goon actor 1] She's done for.
- [cackles]

489
00:21:27,077 --> 00:21:28,912
- Let's go!
- Let's go.

490
00:21:28,996 --> 00:21:32,124
[pensive music playing]

491
00:21:32,207 --> 00:21:34,126
They're going to kill Mama?

492
00:21:34,209 --> 00:21:37,754
[music swells, concludes]

493
00:21:37,838 --> 00:21:39,131
Ah, is everything ready?

494
00:21:39,214 --> 00:21:41,174
Okay. I want your fight scene
to look good.

495
00:21:41,258 --> 00:21:42,592
- [in English] Yes, Director!
- I want it in one take!

496
00:21:42,676 --> 00:21:44,344
- Straight through!
- [in English] One take, Director!

497
00:21:44,428 --> 00:21:46,596
- Okay, Director!
- I'll check over there.

498
00:21:46,680 --> 00:21:48,724
[director] Hey! Fix your shots!

499
00:21:48,807 --> 00:21:51,310
- [director] Okay, let's rehearse!
- Direct-- Director, this is where it goes.

500
00:21:51,393 --> 00:21:52,978
This is a gun, Director, a gun.

501
00:21:53,061 --> 00:21:55,022
Okay. You at the back, react, talents.

502
00:21:55,605 --> 00:21:57,190
- [director, in English] Rehearsing!
- Here, two guns.

503
00:21:57,274 --> 00:21:59,234
- [in English] Okay.
- [in English] Five, four, three, two.

504
00:21:59,318 --> 00:22:01,153
[in English] And action!

505
00:22:01,236 --> 00:22:02,362
[in English] Action!

506
00:22:02,446 --> 00:22:04,239
I'll do this, then this.

507
00:22:04,323 --> 00:22:06,783
- [thumping and grunting]
- [screaming and panicking]

508
00:22:06,867 --> 00:22:08,618
Then I'll block this.

509
00:22:08,702 --> 00:22:10,203
Then I'll do this!

510
00:22:10,287 --> 00:22:11,371
[grunts and groans]

511
00:22:11,455 --> 00:22:12,914
I'll throw like this!

512
00:22:12,998 --> 00:22:15,083
- [screaming]
- Run away now! Run!

513
00:22:15,167 --> 00:22:16,626
That's it, Director! That's it!

514
00:22:16,710 --> 00:22:17,919
Go, go! Run!

515
00:22:18,003 --> 00:22:19,379
[in English] And cut it!

516
00:22:19,463 --> 00:22:24,259
[pleasant music playing]

517
00:22:24,968 --> 00:22:26,470
Ah, excuse me.

518
00:22:26,553 --> 00:22:28,263
Have you seen my mother?

519
00:22:28,346 --> 00:22:29,639
Children aren't allowed here.

520
00:22:30,223 --> 00:22:31,600
Please help me.

521
00:22:31,683 --> 00:22:33,226
They're going to kill my mother!

522
00:22:33,310 --> 00:22:35,687
Go to the police.

523
00:22:35,771 --> 00:22:37,272
No one's being killed here.

524
00:22:37,856 --> 00:22:39,941
There is, believe me!

525
00:22:40,025 --> 00:22:41,943
[gunshots in distance]

526
00:22:42,027 --> 00:22:44,654
[sneaky music playing]

527
00:22:44,738 --> 00:22:49,910
- [thumping and grunting]
- [screaming and panicking]

528
00:22:56,041 --> 00:22:58,085
Run now! Run!

529
00:22:58,168 --> 00:22:59,419
[screaming and panicking]

530
00:22:59,503 --> 00:23:00,462
- What are you doing there?!
- [grunts]

531
00:23:00,545 --> 00:23:01,630
Chase her!

532
00:23:01,713 --> 00:23:04,091
[grunts] I'll kill you!

533
00:23:04,174 --> 00:23:09,179
- [action music playing]
- [screaming and panicking]

534
00:23:12,099 --> 00:23:14,976
[whimpering]

535
00:23:15,060 --> 00:23:18,230
[foreboding music playing]

536
00:23:18,313 --> 00:23:19,564
Mama!

537
00:23:19,648 --> 00:23:20,607
[music swells]

538
00:23:20,690 --> 00:23:21,983
[grunts]

539
00:23:27,322 --> 00:23:29,491
[gasping]

540
00:23:31,743 --> 00:23:32,786
- [man] What happened?
- [director, in English] I'm so sorry.

541
00:23:32,869 --> 00:23:33,995
[in English] I-- I can explain!

542
00:23:34,079 --> 00:23:35,247
[in English] Hey! Cut!

543
00:23:35,330 --> 00:23:37,457
[director] What's happening here?!

544
00:23:37,541 --> 00:23:40,377
[electronic blipping]

545
00:23:40,460 --> 00:23:43,630
[tense music playing]

546
00:23:48,051 --> 00:23:49,177
I spoke to the child.

547
00:23:49,261 --> 00:23:51,471
[Atoy on the phone]
<i>Why didn't you tell her about your job?</i>

548
00:23:51,555 --> 00:23:53,598
And you left her alone at home.

549
00:23:53,682 --> 00:23:54,808
Sorry!

550
00:23:54,891 --> 00:23:56,476
Your setup is amazing.

551
00:23:56,560 --> 00:23:58,228
- [in English] Co-parenting?
- Hey!

552
00:23:58,311 --> 00:23:59,688
Could he be the father?

553
00:23:59,771 --> 00:24:00,689
[Olga] <i>That Ibyang…</i>

554
00:24:00,772 --> 00:24:02,899
<i>She'll answer to me later,</i>
<i>when I get home.</i>

555
00:24:02,983 --> 00:24:04,401
[Janine] Because when…

556
00:24:04,484 --> 00:24:07,154
I saw the shoes of Uncle Red's friend,

557
00:24:07,779 --> 00:24:11,658
they were the same as the shoes
of the man who tried to take me before.

558
00:24:11,741 --> 00:24:12,868
[Audrey] <i>Tell me.</i>

559
00:24:13,493 --> 00:24:15,787
Do you know the man
who tried to take my child?

560
00:24:15,871 --> 00:24:17,205
UP NEXT

561
00:24:17,289 --> 00:24:18,456
[man, in English] Scammer!

562
00:24:18,540 --> 00:24:19,624
[panting]

563
00:24:19,708 --> 00:24:21,168
Mama?

564
00:24:23,920 --> 00:24:25,839
- [grunts]
- Are you okay, my love?

565
00:24:26,840 --> 00:24:28,300
[in English] We will proceed as planned.

566
00:24:28,383 --> 00:24:31,428
[in English] But remember, the decoder
must be taken alive.

567
00:24:31,511 --> 00:24:33,221
[Samir, in English] <i>He might be here too.</i>

568
00:24:33,305 --> 00:24:37,184
[in English] <i>Be careful.</i>
<i>This man has many faces</i>

569
00:24:37,267 --> 00:24:38,643
<i>and can be very dangerous.</i>

570
00:24:38,727 --> 00:24:40,687
♪ <i>Holding the scissors</i> ♪

571
00:24:40,770 --> 00:24:43,899
♪ <i>One cut, and it's over</i> ♪

572
00:24:43,982 --> 00:24:45,442
♪ <i>Fix this</i> ♪

573
00:24:45,525 --> 00:24:46,651
Subtitle translation by: Rachel C. Arias
